rue</showPrefix><prefixActivityLevel>false</prefixActivityLevel><prefixStartIndex /><showPrefixes>false</showPrefixes><blankMinWidth>100</blankMinWidth><blankMaxWidth>650</blankMaxWidth><question_xml><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>true</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>true</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>When he was given the option [of retiring|to retire] early, he accepted it gladly. (&lt;i&gt;retire&lt;/i&gt;)</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/9311.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>When he was given the option &lt;b&gt;of retiring&lt;/b&gt; / &lt;b&gt;to retire&lt;/b&gt; early, he accepted it gladly.</modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>true</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>true</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>The rain showed no sign [of stopping], so they decided to call off the match. (&lt;i&gt;stop&lt;/i&gt;)</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/9312.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>The rain showed no sign &lt;b&gt;of stopping&lt;/b&gt;, so they decided to call off the match.</modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>true</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>true</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>I was feeling depressed because of my failure [to lose] any weight during my diet. (&lt;i&gt;lose&lt;/i&gt;)</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/9313.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>I was feeling depressed because of my failure &lt;b&gt;to lose&lt;/b&gt; any weight during my diet.</modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>true</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>true</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>The New Year concert is always popular, so it makes sense [to book] ahead. (&lt;i&gt;book&lt;/i&gt;)</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/9314.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>The New Year concert is always popular, so it makes sense &lt;b&gt;to book&lt;/b&gt; ahead.</modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>false</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>false</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>She seemed very excited by the prospect [of spending] a few months in Italy. (&lt;i&gt;spend&lt;/i&gt;)</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/9315.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>She seemed very excited by the prospect &lt;b&gt;of spending&lt;/b&gt; a few months in Italy.</modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>false</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>false</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>Students have protested against the government’s decision [to increase] university tuition fees. (&lt;i&gt;increase&lt;/i&gt;)</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/9316.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>Students have protested against the government’s decision &lt;b&gt;to increase&lt;/b&gt; university tuition fees.</modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>false</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>false</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>Luke's parents helped him achieve his ambition [of becoming|to become] a professional racing driver. (&lt;i&gt;become&lt;/i&gt;) </text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/9317.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>Luke's parents helped him achieve his ambition &lt;b&gt;of becoming&lt;/b&gt; / &lt;b&gt;to become&lt;/b&gt; a professional racing driver.</modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>false</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>false</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>She had an unusual way [of holding] her pen, but her writing was very elegant. (&lt;i&gt;hold&lt;/i&gt;)</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/9318.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>She had an unusual way &lt;b&gt;of holding&lt;/b&gt; her pen, but her writing was very elegant.</modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>false</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>false</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>I didn't want to take the car into the city centre because of the problem [of finding] somewhere to park. (&lt;i&gt;find&lt;/i&gt;)</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/9319.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>I didn't want to take the car into the city centre because of the problem &lt;b&gt;of finding&lt;/b&gt; somewhere to park.</modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>false</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>false</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>The farmer gave us permission [to put up] our tent in one of his fields. (&lt;i&gt;put up&lt;/i&gt;)</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/93110.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>The farmer gave us permission &lt;b&gt;to put up&lt;/b&gt; our tent in one of h